  {
   "id": "WrRYxRHkAAAJ",
   "from": "Edward Rigdon",
   "author": "99a06696c483481a",
   "date": "2020-04-16T13:35:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: Read in Summary Data (Correlation Matrix)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You could also consider copy and paste to get your lower triangular matrix into R. <div>Here is an example that I use, involving data from Bagozzi (1980) and the </div><div>lavaan package&#39;s getCov() function:<div><br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; library(&quot;lavaan&quot;,\r\nlib.loc=&quot;~/R/win-library/3.6&quot;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\"> </span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; Bagcorstr&lt;-&#39; 1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">   0.418   1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  0.394   0.627  \r\n1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  0.129   0.202  \r\n0.266   1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  0.189   0.284  \r\n0.208   0.365   1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  0.544   0.281  \r\n0.324   0.201   0.161  \r\n1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  0.507   0.225  \r\n0.314   0.172   0.174  \r\n0.546  1.000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">  -0.357  -0.156 \r\n-0.038  -0.199  -0.277 \r\n-0.294 -0.174  1.000&#39;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; Bagnames&lt;-c(&quot;Perform1&quot;, &quot;JobSat1&quot;,\r\n&quot;JobSat2&quot;, &quot;AchMot1&quot;, &quot;AchMot2&quot;,<br>                             &quot;SelfEst1&quot;, &quot;SelfEst2&quot;, &quot;VerbInt1&quot;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; # Use default spec, first indicator loading fixed to 1</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; Bagcor&lt;-getCov(Bagcorstr,names=Bagnames)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\"><br></span></p>This works fine, producing a square, symmetric matrix. (Bagozzi 1980 </div><div>analyzed the correlation matrix, without correction, because the &quot;Perform&quot; variable&#39;s </div><div>variance is about 10,000 times the variances of the other observed variables, and </div><div>analyzing the covariance matrix produces nonconvergence errors.. If you divide </div><div>the &quot;Perform&quot; variable&#39;s standard deviation by 100, you can analyze the covariance matrix</div><div>without a problem.)</div><div><div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\"> </span></p></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Apr 15, 2020 at 9:29 AM Arne Floh &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">arne...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I have problems using a correlation matrix in lavaan. I have read the tutorial on <a href=\"http://lavaan.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421963779000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ShO24q84cIAcjCBobIoau\">lavaan.org</a> and I can replicate the example. However, when I want to read in my LOWER correlation matrix I always get an error message.<div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s my code:</div><div><br></div><div><div>matrix_ex5 &lt;- read_csv(&quot;MASEM/ex5.csv&quot;, col_names = FALSE)</div></div><div>view(matrix_ex5) </div><div><br></div><div>ex5_cov &lt;- getCov(matrix_ex5, names = c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;))<br></div><div><br></div><div>Error code:</div><div>Error in lav_matrix_lower2full(x, diagonal = diagonal) : <br></div><div><div>  p == round(p, 0) is not TRUE</div></div><div><br></div><div>When I read in the matrix and look at it, it seems that R has replaced the upper triangle with NA&#39;s. Not sure if this is causing the error message. Nevertheless, I don&#39;t know how to remove the NA&#39;s of the upper triangle. I have tried packages such as matrixcalc, etc.</div><div><br></div><div>Help appreciated.</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/cb4a4b6b-b804-4990-863c-aecfae2865fb%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/cb4a4b6b-b804-4990-863c-aecfae2865fb%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421963779000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2X2Ofbo1GlzRyoAbPRKSz1\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/cb4a4b6b-b804-4990-863c-aecfae2865fb%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
